Problem: Valid Palindrome II (LC 680)

Pattern: Two Pointers

Approach:

1. Use two pointers, one at the beginning and one at the end.
2. Compare the characters at both pointers.
3. If they are equal, move both pointers inward.
4. If they are different, this is the one character we are allowed to remove.
5. Try skipping the left character and check whether the remaining part is a palindrome.
6. Also try skipping the right character and check whether the remaining part is a palindrome.
7. If either option forms a palindrome, return true.
8. If all characters match without needing a removal, return true.
9. Otherwise, return false.

Key Idea:
At the first mismatch, we get only one chance to remove a character. Check both possible removals.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(n) due to the helper function receiving the string by value.
